stateDiagram-v2
    %% Realm-specific rendering of the shared D-82 Base/Auth admission contract.
    [*] --> issued: parent Visitor flow / binding transaction
    issued --> attached: Auth attaches active session and confirmation reference
    issued --> retired: expiry or explicit restart
    attached --> confirmed: Base confirms nonce digest and root token
    attached --> retired: expiry or cancellation
    confirmed --> redeemed: matching browser-bound Auth session redeems
    confirmed --> retired: expiry or cancellation
    redeemed --> [*]
    retired --> [*]
    note right of issued
        References identify the operation;
        the browser nonce digest is the proof binding.
        No Auth general login session is created.
        Distinct pending parents may share an active sid,
        including continuity admitted for an earlier parent.
        Attachment grants no authority for the new purpose.
        Sign-in path checks the server-fixed effective intent before redemption.
        Issuance stores immutable curfew_at = OP clock + 30 minutes.
        Switch copies that curfew; entry_intent is required and purpose-constrained.
        Re-verification intent is the explicit not_applicable value.
        Curfew storage does not yet replace acceptance/parent expiry consumers.
        GET checks nonce ownership without mutation.
        Transitions use the owning Ticket DB clock.
        Browser receivers lock root owner/device/token when present,
        then the exact parent, binding and Auth rows in ID order.
        Auth cookies are written only after Ticket commit.
        Binding collection waits for every sign-up Flow to be terminal,
        physically purgeable, and cleanup completed or registration completed.
        Flow rows are deleted before their restrictive Binding.
    end note
